[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/murakumo now exposes ComfyUI over plain HTTP (POST /v1/images/generations, POST /workflows/run, PRs #7/#8) instead of SSH-loopback-only, backed by the fleet's real Mac-mini nodes (zebulun/benjamin hold animagine-xl-4.0.safetensors); ~5-8 min/image on this Apple Silicon CPU/Metal hardware" "PR #9 fixed a real scheduling bug found via live testing: an omitted :model in an image request left :model/checkpoint nil, which schedule/eligible? treats as every :comfyui node being eligible regardless of actual checkpoint (including video-only nodes) -- both endpoints now default to animagine-xl-4.0.safetensors (MURAKUMO_DEFAULT_IMAGE_CKPT override)" "gateway + VOICEVOX Engine 0.25.2 (official macOS-arm64 native release, downloaded and installed to ~/.murakumo/voicevox-engine/run) are both persisted as per-user LaunchAgents on main-2.local (com.murakumo.infer-gateway, com.murakumo.voicevox-engine) -- survive logout/reboot, self-heal on crash; LaunchAgents need explicit PATH in EnvironmentVariables since they don't inherit shell PATH" "gateway reachable via localhost AND the operator machine's Tailscale IP (100.108.223.94:8790) with no additional exposure step -- public-internet exposure (Cloudflare Tunnel) deliberately not set up, remains a separate decision" "first real NIST video produced end-to-end: cyber-ep-055 (content/cyber-nist-csf-yougo.edn series, 26 episodes total), via a one-off scratchpad script (NOT yet a committed graph executor) -- real VOICEVOX narration (26 lines) + real ComfyUI backgrounds (6 scenes, animagine-xl-4.0) + PIL-burned captions (this machine's ffmpeg has no drawtext/libass, confirmed via `ffmpeg -filters`) + ffmpeg assembly -> ~/Movies/yukkuri-nist-output/cyber-ep-055-assertion.mp4 (5m03s, 5.0MB)" "known incomplete/follow-up items: (1) no character overlay -- a character-plan generation attempt timed out; root cause is character-workflow's default checkpoint (waiIllustriousSDXL_v160.safetensors) not matching 